node_modules/next/dist/docs/02-pages/02-guides/upgrading/version-11.md:136:React 17 introduced a new [JSX Transform](https://reactjs.org/blog/2020/09/22/introducing-the-new-jsx-transform.html) that brings a long-time Next.js feature to the wider React ecosystem: Not having to `import React from 'react'` when using JSX. When using React 17 Next.js will automatically use the new transform. This transform does not make the `React` variable global, which was an unintended side-effect of the previous Next.js implementation. A [codemod is available](/docs/pages/guides/upgrading/codemods#add-missing-react-import) to automatically fix cases where you accidentally used `React` without importing it.
