2. **The cleanup strategy is incomplete for changing var sets.** The plan says `SiteThemeVars` covers all 21 tokens, but also says leave `--destructive*` unset when error is absent. If error exists while enabled, then is removed, stale inline destructive vars will remain unless the hook removes previously applied keys before applying the next set. Either emit a complete token set every time or track/remove previous keys on every update, not only on OFF/unmount.

3. **Restore should snapshot previous inline values, not only `removeProperty`.** Today there is no runtime root theme, but “restores exactly” is stronger than “remove what we set.” If any pre-existing inline custom property exists on `<html>`, removing it is wrong. Snapshot `{ value, priority, existed }` before first apply and restore on cleanup.

