6. **The contrast claim is too broad.** Existing `readableTextColor` only chooses `#111111` or white for a single background [lib/color.ts](/home/vernon/Projects/Local/ui-color-picker-preview/lib/color.ts:229). It does not validate all semantic pairs. In particular, planned `--muted ← neutral-500` can fail AA on `neutral-50` surfaces; gray `#858585` on `#f7f7f7` is about 3.44:1. Tests must cover `foreground/background`, `muted/surface`, `secondary`, `accent`, `accent-subtle`, `destructive`, hover, and dialog text pairs.

7. **Accent mapping is underspecified.** There is no `accent` preset in [lib/theme.ts](/home/vernon/Projects/Local/ui-color-picker-preview/lib/theme.ts:21). The preview has a positional `accent` alias only as the fifth role [lib/color.ts](/home/vernon/Projects/Local/ui-color-picker-preview/lib/color.ts:313). Define whether accent means tertiary, fifth palette, custom name “Accent,” or primary fallback.

